# {{PRODUCT}} — GitHub Copilot / VS Code

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`. The rules file wins.

- Run harness scripts with `{{PY}}` (never assume `python3` on Windows).
- Use the central policy to select only the required reviewers and gates, then bind their evidence to the final snapshot.
- Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_gradle_task.py {{ASSEMBLE}}`
- Independent Reviews: Required reviewer roles must be evaluated independently; lead agents must never self-certify reviews with `record_review.py --verdict PASS` on HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes.
- Zero-Polling Invariant: Never poll background tasks or subagents in a loop. Yield execution and wait for reactive messages.
- Review Ingestion: Ingest reviewer responses with `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --from-subagent <role>=<convId>` or `--response-text "<name>=<text>"`.
- Task Resumption: Run `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py resume --repo . --task-id <id>` if BLOCKED or for fixes.
- Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}}
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough: After every device installation (`run_device.py install-start`), the agent MUST output a complete, numbered mobile verification walkthrough (Navigation path, Preconditions, User actions, Expected results, Edge cases) in chat BEFORE asking the developer for verification. Never ask if it passed without detailing test steps.
- {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Safety enforcement: this repo registers a Copilot `preToolUse` hook
  (`.github/hooks/android-harness-pre-tool-use.json`) that deterministically denies
  git mutations, emulator tooling, and unsafe adb commands. Do not try to bypass it.
  If the hook file is absent (older checkout, hook support unavailable), treat
  `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/pre_tool_safety.py` as the reference policy: apply the same
  denials yourself before every shell command (best-effort). The hook can hard-enforce covered mutations, but conversational approval remains `RULE_ENFORCED`; read the detected tier from `_product.py` and do not claim cryptographic human separation.

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Step | Canonical Command | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Discovery** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/project_graph.py --feature <name>` (or `--find <Symbol>`) | Fast AST/symbol project graph analysis |
| **Clarification** | Interactive question with developer before drafting plan |
| **Context Note** | `{{PY}} harness_cli.py context note "<note>"` | Record architectural convention/note |
| **Preflight Gate** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/preflight.py` (or `preflight_check.py`) | Deterministic check: room, fast ktlint, string parity |
| **Unit Tests** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_tests_gate.py` | Run unit tests gate |
| **Review Package** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/review_package.py` | Generate immutable review package markdown |
| **Review Harvest** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --from-subagent <role>=<convId>` | Auto-harvest subagent transcript and record review |
| **Review Text** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --response-text "<role>=<text>"` | Direct review text ingestion with evidence footer |
| **Resume Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py resume --repo . --task-id <id>` | Resume task from BLOCKED or VERIFYING back to implementation |
| **Assemble Debug** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_gradle_task.py {{ASSEMBLE}}` | Build debug APK (ONLY after all reviewers pass) |
| **Device Deploy** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_device.py install-start` | Install and launch on target device/emulator |
| **Screen Capture** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/capture_screen.py --output-name <name>` | Capture device screen for verification proof |
| **Final Verify** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py verify --repo . --task-id <id>` | Read-only delivery verification check |
| **Deliver Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py deliver --repo . --task-id <id>` | Finalize delivery state after git commit |
